# **✅ FIXED! The Bug Was Found! 🔥**

## **What Was Wrong:**

The UI code was checking:
```javascript
if (!data || !Array.isArray(data) || data.length === 0)
```

But the API returns:
```json
{
  "conversations": [...]
}
```

So `data` is an **object**, not an array! The check failed and showed "No conversations yet."

## **The Fix:**

```javascript
const conversations = data.conversations || data;
```

Now it extracts the `conversations` array from the response object.

